1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,413
This is SiteMind: a durable procurement agent for construction.

2
00:00:04,443 --> 00:00:10,921
On a 24 MW data-centre job, long-lead 480 V switchgear is the number-one
schedule risk.

3
00:00:10,951 --> 00:00:16,919
Today, coordinators juggle quotes, lead times and budgets in email and
Excel, for weeks.

4
00:00:16,949 --> 00:00:22,746
Project Alpha is a Tier-III build at Chakan, Pune, and one missed date
slips energisation.

5
00:00:24,117 --> 00:00:27,137
We hand SiteMind one goal, in plain English.

6
00:00:27,167 --> 00:00:35,049
Order the 480 V switchgear for Project Alpha by 15 March 2027, within ₹4.6 crore.

7
00:00:36,017 --> 00:00:42,166
A local model on this laptop drafts the plan: a task graph with deadlines,
budget and risks.

8
00:00:42,196 --> 00:00:44,276
Fourteen tasks, five risks.

9
00:00:44,306 --> 00:00:49,265
Each step is assigned to a specialist agent, and the simulated clock
starts on day one.

10
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:56,524
The takeoff specialist reads the switchgear spec PDF and extracts every
line item, with its source.

11
00:00:56,554 --> 00:01:01,580
It finds eight items, and flags one mismatch against the drawing for an RFI.

12
00:01:01,610 --> 00:01:06,703
Then requests for quotation go out to three mock vendors, each sent
exactly once.

13
00:01:06,733 --> 00:01:08,993
The vendors and prices are synthetic.

14
00:01:09,983 --> 00:01:15,668
Real vendors are messy. Voltaris times out twice; the agent backs off and retries.

15
00:01:15,698 --> 00:01:22,668
Kestrel then revises its price up fourteen percent, a copper surcharge
plus a lost discount, which breaks the budget.

16
00:01:22,698 --> 00:01:27,724
SiteMind notices, and re-plans to version two instead of blindly continuing.

17
00:01:28,717 --> 00:01:32,862
Now the hard part. We kill the worker process, mid-run, with SIGKILL.

18
00:01:32,892 --> 00:01:36,085
No graceful shutdown. The agent is simply gone.

19
00:01:41,717 --> 00:01:46,628
A fresh worker resumes from the last LangGraph checkpoint, saved after every task.

20
00:01:46,658 --> 00:01:53,574
The action ledger shows it: every action appears once, and anything
requested twice was still executed only once.

21
00:01:53,604 --> 00:01:56,935
No duplicate emails. No duplicate orders.

22
00:01:57,917 --> 00:02:02,403
Before anything that can't be undone, SiteMind stops and asks a person.

23
00:02:02,433 --> 00:02:13,649
The decision memo ranks every option on cost, delivery float and
reliability, and recommends one: Anvil's expedited slot, ₹26 lakh extra,
on site before the deadline.

24
00:02:13,679 --> 00:02:16,436
Voltaris is cheaper, but would arrive late.

25
00:02:16,466 --> 00:02:18,486
The project manager approves it.

26
00:02:19,450 --> 00:02:29,837
It drafts the purchase order, asks once more before release, then sends it
exactly once: ₹4.7 crore with GST, 33 days ahead of the order-by date.

27
00:02:29,867 --> 00:02:33,707
Every decision, specialist call and rupee is in the audit trail.

28
00:02:34,683 --> 00:02:38,424
Weeks of chasing, down to minutes. Every decision audited.

29
00:02:38,454 --> 00:02:45,041
It survives crashes without repeating itself, and it is open source,
running on a laptop with a local model.

30
00:02:45,071 --> 00:02:46,119
SiteMind.
